From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:14:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] runtime: defer imported-table function reference
 materialization

Retain immutable active-segment function indices in shared module metadata
and bounded source/range bindings on imported function tables. Preserve
bounds checks, segment order and fuel at initialization while materializing
VMFuncRef records through existing lazy reads. Explicit writes retain their
initialized tags; unsupported forms and bounded-history overflow stay eager.

Keep source instances alive through the Store's existing ownership,
including failed initialization. Resolve overlapping copies before writing
and discard binding history when pooled tables are recycled. Internal
segment initialization must not introduce embedder call-hook transitions.

Advance mandatory native metadata versions so prior Module layouts and
builtin contracts are rejected even without optional version-string checks.
Portable Core WebAssembly and its imports remain unchanged.

Validation: source ownership/aliasing review, eager/lazy table semantics,
overlap and explicit null writes, failed and repeated initialization,
serialized reload, call-hook behavior, mandatory old-artifact rejection,
and sustained application replay with matching outputs.
